                </div>

                <!-- Q8: Empire Expansion Short Answer -->
                <div class="glass-card rounded-xl p-6 mb-6">
                    <div class="flex justify-between items-start mb-3">
                        <span class="text-xs font-bold text-rose-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Question 8 • 6 Marks</span>
                        <span class="text-xs text-slate-400">Synthesis Explanation</span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-slate-200 font-medium text-sm md:text-base mb-2">
                        How did the combination of <strong>paved roads</strong>, <strong>coastal forts</strong>, and <strong>sea routes (Mare Nostrum)</strong> allow the Roman army to conquer lands and control a giant empire?
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mb-4">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb text-amber-400 mr-1"></i>
                        <em>Tip: Mention fast movement of legions (~30km/day), moving supplies/grain by ship, or building forts at strategic locations.</em>
                    </p>
                    <textarea id="q8-response" rows="4" placeholder="Explain how roads, seas, and forts worked together..." class="w-full bg-slate-900 border border-slate-700 rounded-lg p-3 text-slate-200 text-sm focus:outline-none focus:border-rose-500 transition"></textarea>
